[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120471 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119953 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "76437951-0d71-548b-b330-e494aa12c6a1" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Geometric Sequences" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048829 :topic/id #uuid "c4140dd8-d457-5cdb-8b51-1b7b952642cd" :topic/math-academy-id 1818 :topic/title "The Recursive Formula for a Geometric Sequence"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "390c1fb2-1a90-5dca-ab06-3d62261b8d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460011} {:answer/id #uuid "3016aa58-a310-5be6-abf5-ca2c21e4a3ab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460012}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "390c1fb2-1a90-5dca-ab06-3d62261b8d19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460011} :answer-field/id #uuid "519a912c-8ed4-5161-98e7-b511fdd9ec3e" :answer-field/key "$5,\\,10,\\,15,\\,…$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460872} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05fee7a0-539a-5fd8-bf1c-0b6ff426d762" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460013} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d18fb0-4f09-536f-ae5b-55474e02470b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d4d18fb0-4f09-536f-ae5b-55474e02470b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460014} :answer-field/id #uuid "4707ce5a-9d1b-5b75-8e18-487da0841c95" :answer-field/key "${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=18,\\,n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460873} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9335fe-a0f8-5da8-93e5-e265aeb82f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460015} {:answer/id #uuid "3783a2e7-ec7a-56cf-b5b9-895dc2990505" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460016}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9335fe-a0f8-5da8-93e5-e265aeb82f19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460015} :answer-field/id #uuid "5759d221-2f33-5ccc-b175-b5e7ddf2e21f" :answer-field/key "$f(n+1)=2f(n)+3$, $f(1)=1$, $n\\ge 1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186460874}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8e320c2f-640c-53dc-a6d6-b04a67d6047a" :question/math-academy-id "q-44824" :question/problem "Which of the three sequences below are geometric sequences?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A sequence is geometric if there is a common ratio between its terms. Let's check each sequence in turn.\n\n- Sequence $5,\\,10,\\,15,\\,…$ is not geometric because not every pair of consecutive terms has the same ratio. To see this, we only need to go up to the third term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{10}{5} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{15}{10} & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Sequence ${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=18,\\,n\\ge 1$ is a geometric sequence. The recursive rule ${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n}$ tells us that each term is $6$ times the previous term, so the common ratio is $r=6.$\n\n- Sequence $f(n+1)=2f(n)+3,\\,f(1)=1,\\,n\\ge 1$ is not a geometric sequence. To see this, we can calculate the first $3$ terms of the sequence and then compute the ratios of consecutive terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1) & =1 \\\\ f(2) & =2\\cdot 1+3=5 \\\\ f(3) & =2\\cdot 5+3=13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the first two pairs of consecutive terms have different ratios:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{f(2)}{f(1)}=\\frac{5}{1} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{f(3)}{f(2)}=\\frac{13}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn conclusion, only sequence ${a}_{n+1}=6{a}_{n},\\,{a}_{1}=18,\\,n\\ge 1$ is a geometric sequence." :step/_content [{:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/title "Mathematics for Machine Learning: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419031} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419100} {:activity/_steps {:activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046658} :activity/title "Mathematics for Machine Learning: Placement Exam" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045462 :db/ident :activity.type/diagnostic} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557865} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186558641}]} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125242 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124589 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "099e7caf-085a-5fd5-ad3d-1ebf189527b7" :knowledge-point/title "Verifying Properties Involving Scalar Multiplication and the Distributive Laws" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049737 :topic/id #uuid "0f66ea93-6fdc-5bbf-826c-7d07b2ef17d7" :topic/math-academy-id 1906 :topic/title "Introduction to Abstract Vector Spaces"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0f6fb82-50a8-5852-bf40-a37479778409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448804} {:answer/id #uuid "9267a6f1-3504-5a32-96b0-ac1372955011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9267a6f1-3504-5a32-96b0-ac1372955011" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448805} :answer-field/id #uuid "84410673-cc05-5a6f-b9ee-75274828699f" :answer-field/key "The scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ is associative." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449442} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "abad889d-1c90-5258-9739-fee99698474e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448806} {:answer/id #uuid "25dda0f1-64d9-5c8b-b93e-f7f8e89336b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448807}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25dda0f1-64d9-5c8b-b93e-f7f8e89336b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448807} :answer-field/id #uuid "32ac74a8-70ee-5e3d-b945-366ffa92576a" :answer-field/key "For any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$ and $f(x)\\in L,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449443} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a729165e-39d5-598d-8061-7d0c6882ab7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448808} {:answer/id #uuid "84f6c2b7-2f40-5d2c-9188-36685b487210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84f6c2b7-2f40-5d2c-9188-36685b487210" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448809} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ed18b92-c4e7-57b6-b603-49203e853cfd" :answer-field/key "For any $\\alpha \\in R$ and any $f(x),g(x)\\in L,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))$ $=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449444}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bd415fe2-3ead-5cbb-88ba-59d9d1273317" :question/math-academy-id "q-94740" :question/problem "Let $L$ be the set of all functions from $(0,\\infty )$ to $R$ of the form $f(x)=a{log}_{2}⁡(x),$ where $a\\in R.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's examine each of our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement “The scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ is associative” is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n\\alpha (\\beta f(x))=(\\alpha \\beta )f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$ and $f(x)\\in L,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R,$ we obtain that\n\n$$\n(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).\n$$\n\n- Statement “For any $\\alpha \\in R$ and any $f(x),g(x)\\in L,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$” is true. Indeed, for any $f(x)\\in L$ and for any fixed $x\\in (0,\\infty ),$ the result of $f(x)$ is just a real number. Thus, for any $\\alpha \\in R,$ we obtain that \n\n$$\n\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “The scalar multiplication of functions in $L$ is associative”; “For any $\\alpha ,\\beta \\in R$ and $f(x)\\in L,$ we have $(\\alpha +\\beta )f(x)=\\alpha f(x)+\\beta f(x).$”; “For any $\\alpha \\in R$ and any $f(x),g(x)\\in L,$ we have $\\alpha (f(x)+g(x))=\\alpha f(x)+\\alpha g(x).$”."}]
